      <!--Q#9-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para> What is the point of intersection of the two lines? </para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para> \((10, 300)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q#12-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para> Talk with your partner. What does this intersection mean in the context of the problem? </para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>At 10 visits, the cost is the same at $300.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q#13-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para> Write a paragraph to describe when Option A is better and when Option B is better. Share your paragraph with your partner. Read each other’s paragraphs and then discuss if you agree or disagree. </para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. The two options cost the same at 10 visits. Since Option A is less money up front, Option A will be less expensive until the 10th visit. After 10 visits, however, Option B is less expensive. </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
